23. ORDER VALIDATION

OrderIntent
 ↓
Schema validation
 ↓
Account validation
 ↓
Position validation
 ↓
Capital validation
 ↓
Risk validation
 ↓
Authority validation
 ↓
Market condition validation
 ↓
Provider validation
 ↓
Duplicate check
 ↓
Execution


---

24. IDEMPOTENCY

Every executable action receives an idempotency key.

same request
+
same idempotency key
        ↓
duplicate detected
        ↓
do not blindly execute twice

This protects against:

retries

crashes

network duplication

provider timeout ambiguity



---

25. ORDER LIFECYCLE

CREATED
 ↓
VALIDATING
 ↓
APPROVED
 ↓
SUBMITTED
 ↓
ACKNOWLEDGED
 ↓
PARTIALLY_FILLED
 ↓
FILLED

Alternative states:

REJECTED
CANCEL_REQUESTED
CANCELLED
EXPIRED
FAILED
UNKNOWN


---

26. PARTIAL FILL / CANCEL-REPLACE

Execution must track:

filled_quantity
remaining_quantity
average_fill_price
execution_attempt
cancel_replace_version

Example:

100 shares requested
 ↓
40 filled
 ↓
60 remaining
 ↓
risk state updated
 ↓
cancel / replace / continue

A partial fill is a new financial state, not merely an intermediate message.


---

27. UNKNOWN EXECUTION STATE

Critical rule:

UNKNOWN
≠
FILLED
≠
FAILED

If broker/execution-provider response is uncertain:

QUERY PROVIDER
 ↓
RECONCILE
 ↓
UPDATE CANONICAL STATE

Never blindly retry an unknown order.


---

28. EXECUTION RECONCILIATION

INTERNAL STATE
       ↕
EXTERNAL PROVIDER
       ↓
COMPARE
       ↓
MATCH
OR
DISCREPANCY
       ↓
INVESTIGATE
       ↓
CORRECT
       ↓
RECORD

This is mandatory for live operation.


