29. FINANCIAL LEDGER / ACCOUNTING AUTHORITY

This is the authoritative record of financial events.

FinancialEvent {
    event_id
    account_id
    instrument_id?
    event_type
    quantity?
    price?
    amount
    currency
    fees[]
    tax[]
    source
    timestamp
    provenance
    idempotency_key
}

Events may include:

trade

fee

tax

dividend

corporate_action

deposit

withdrawal

financing

adjustment

cash movement


Financial state is reconstructed from durable financial events and reconciled against external account state; P&L is calculated from financial events together with the applicable valuation/market data and cost records.


---

30. P&L

P&L must distinguish:

realized P&L

unrealized P&L

fees

taxes

slippage

financing

other costs


Research must support:

gross performance

net performance


They must never be silently conflated.


---

31. LIQUIDITY AND CAPACITY

The system must distinguish:

THEORETICAL POSITION

from:

EXECUTABLE POSITION

A strategy may theoretically request a large position while actual market liquidity makes that position impractical.

Capacity evaluation considers:

volume

spread

depth

expected impact

order size

market participation

time-to-execute



